+verdict: don't merge
+issue_repro: fail
+branch_tests: pass
+test_checks_the_fix: no
+
+Why: The branch joins a quoted line with the next one, but it never strips the
+trailing carriage return that Windows line endings leave on every line. Running
+the issue's own repro on the branch gives 3 rows, but the note field is
+`call back\r\nafter 5pm"\r`, not the expected `call back\r\nafter 5pm`; the
+header and other fields also keep stray `\r` and `"` characters (for example
+`note\r` and `no notes"\r`). Quoted commas are still split too.
+
+The new test uses LF-only input (`'1,"a\nb",x\n'`) with nothing after the
+closing quote, so it passes even though the reported CRLF bug is unfixed; it
+covers only the simpler LF case. Its second assertion even freezes the existing
+broken quoted-comma behavior as expected (`'1,"x, y",z\n'` must yield four
+fields), so a correct fix would have to break it. The branch's suite is green
+(2 tests), but that green run is not evidence that #42 is fixed.
+
+Neither branch was modified; checks ran in throwaway detached worktrees outside
+the repository.
